# React Conventions

## Components

- Functional components and hooks only (no class components)
- One component per file
- PascalCase for component filenames (e.g. `ProjectCard.tsx`)
- Keep components small and focused; extract when a file does too much
- Prefer TypeScript (`.ts` / `.tsx`) for all new and migrated source

## File layout

| Location | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `src/pages/` | Page-level route components |
| `src/components/` | Shared / reusable UI components |
| `src/components/pinup/` | Home PinUpBoard engine (board, cards, connectors, coords) |
| `src/data/` | Content as plain arrays/objects |
| `src/data/pinUpBoardData/` | Home board cards: folder tree mirrors the mind-map; one `*Card.tsx` per node; parent `index.ts` explicitly registers children |

Never hardcode page content inside page components — put it in `src/data/` (or `pinUpBoardData` for board cards) and import it.

### PinUpBoard cards

Follow `.cursor/rules/pinup-board-data.mdc` when adding or changing board cards/branches.

Quick leaf-card checklist: new `*Card.tsx` → export `BoardCardModule` → register in branch `index.ts`.  
Quick new-branch checklist: hub + list folder + branch `index.ts` → wire into `pinUpBoardData/index.ts`.

## Comments and editable content

- Comment non-obvious code
- Mark user-editable content with `EDIT ME` so it is easy to find and change

## Accessibility

- Use semantic HTML (`main`, `nav`, `section`, headings in order)
- Provide meaningful `alt` text for images
- Support keyboard navigation
- Keep focus states visible (do not remove outline without a clear replacement)
